# The 2026-08-24 bindings. Listed BY NAME rather than as `mojolearn/*.so`,
# keeping this file's existing shape: a glob would also swallow a .so that
# someone genuinely meant to track, and the explicit list is what makes a
# forgotten binding show up as untracked instead of vanishing silently.
mojolearn/_mojolearn_svm.so
mojolearn/_mojolearn_solver.so
mojolearn/_mojolearn_metrics.so
mojolearn/_mojolearn_tsa.so
mojolearn/_mojolearn_linalg.so
# The 2026-09-01 bindings. BOTH WERE MISSING and the older one had already
# been COMMITTED as a 625K binary in `cc269dca` before anybody noticed --
# which is this file's own comment above coming true. The explicit list makes
# a forgotten binding show up as untracked; it only works if somebody adds
# the line when the binding lands, and twice in a row nobody did. Untracked
# forward in the commit that added these lines, not rewritten out of history.
mojolearn/_mojolearn_arima.so
mojolearn/_mojolearn_training.so
# The gp binding (2026-09-01, the thirteenth). Third instance of the same
# omission this file's comments predict: the binding shipped green and the
# .so sat untracked until the phase-8 rent pre-flight refused the dirty
# tree. Added the same day, forward.
mojolearn/_mojolearn_gp.so
# The mamba binding (2026-09-01, the fourteenth). FOURTH instance: the
# surface lane shipped green the same evening the gp line above was added
# for the third instance, and still forgot its own line. Found the next
# morning by the same signal as always -- the .so untracked in status.
mojolearn/_mojolearn_mamba.so
# Build output copied in by packaging/macos/build_release_wheel.sh so that
# `python -m mojolearn verify` has a comparator inside the wheel. The single
# source stays tools/identity_trace_diff.py in git.
mojolearn/_identity_trace_diff.py
